rk completion, zero exit status, or clean-state verification.\\n@@\\n A serialized success alone does not prove the pipeline is defective: it also\\n@@\\n outcome before drawing either conclusion.\\n+\\n+This successful run shows that the segment storage can complete this workload\\n+when copy/decode execution is serialized. The leading investigation area is\\n+the interaction of pipelined execution with segment/metadata/ring reuse, rather\\n+than treating the crash location inside libcuda as attribution to NVIDIA.\\n+It does not establish which event dependency, lifetime, or driver interaction\\n+is responsible. The Measure-window mean load-candidate count changed from\\n+1,649 in the original to 2,372 in this run, so the runs do not have identical\\n+live KV state. One successful run is not a general fix or a performance claim.\\n+\\n+The original eight-cell launcher remains in normal pipeline mode. The new\\n+diagnostic option is opt-in and is not enabled by that launcher.\\n*** Update File: /home/ubuntu/tieredserve-crash-analysis.md\\n@@\\n ## Conclusion\\n \\n+An authorized follow-up diagnostic has now completed: keeping segment storage\\n+but submitting K/V H2D and decode on one CUDA stream allowed all 1,200 requests\\n+at rate 1.4 to finish with no request errors or crash. Nsight confirmed H2D and\\n+batched CD3 decode on the same stream. Details and results are in\\n+`/home/ubuntu/cd3-serial-diagnostic/README.md`. This narrows the investigation\\n+toward pipeline/lifetime interactions but does not establish the precise bug.\\n+\\n@@\\n-Production source, experiment settings, and installed libraries were not\\n-changed during this diagnosis. No serving experiment was restarted.\\n+The initial core-only diagnosis did not change production source or restart\\n+serving. After the user explicitly authorized the serialization experiment,\\n+an opt-in diagnostic was added and the failing 1.4 cell was run once. Normal\\n+pipeline defaults remain unchanged. Original 